---
name: presence-recovery
description: Agent work pauses after sustained absence and ends on removal.
engine: 0.2.0-lab.1
roles: [requester, assistant]
extensions: [host.presence/1, host.membership/1]
---
"""
One assistant works on one question while the room watches presence. Sustained
absence pauses the work instead of failing it; removal from the room ends it.
Presence is a host signal, not proof that work is or is not happening.
"""
contract @infinity => expired

watch supervisor

"""
Ask one question and wait. A pause means the assistant or supervisor went
offline; it is not an answer and not a failure. A pause ends the open question:
ask it again once the assistant is back.
"""
role requester

"""
Answer the question. If you were offline, say so when you come back and continue
from what you already had; do not restart silently.
"""
role assistant

"""
One question, with the context needed to answer it.
"""
type question
  text: text(2000)

"""
The answer, noting any interruption that may have affected it. Set question to
the question you answer.
"""
type answer
  question: ref(question)
  text: text(4000)

"""
The requester asks its question.
"""
state new
  """
  Ask the question. The assistant then owes one answer to it.
  """
  requester -> assistant: question() awaits working
    """
    The assistant answers within ten minutes of the question.
    """
    => answer() & complete
     """
     No answer arrived within ten minutes of the question.
     """
     | @10m & stalled

"""
The assistant works while present. Five minutes offline, for the assistant or
the watched supervisor, pauses the work and ends the open question. The question
can be asked at most four times.
"""
state working max_entries 4 => stalled
  on assistant offline for 5m => paused
  on watch.supervisor offline for 5m => paused

"""
Work is paused for absence, and the question is no longer owed. The pause lasts
until the assistant returns; after three pauses the session stalls.
"""
state paused max_entries 3 => stalled
  on assistant online => resumed

"""
The assistant is back. The requester asks the question again within ten minutes,
and the assistant then owes a fresh answer.
"""
state resumed @10m => stalled
  """
  Ask the same question again. The assistant answers it within ten minutes.
  """
  requester -> assistant: question() => working

"""
In any state, removing the assistant from the room ends the session.
"""
anystate
  on assistant removed => left

"""
An answer arrived; the requester still judges it.
"""
end complete

"""
No answer in time, no question again in time, or too many pauses. The requester
decides how to recover.
"""
end stalled

"""
The assistant left the room; nothing more will arrive in this session.
"""
end left
